{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016ZWLHzsFbTjhoTj885jmPc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NxNsXMw6r1EgZowBfYPUkL","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a8f24532f93ac9baa","message":"## Step 2: Cross-Sharing\n\nReviewer 2 (focusing on novelty and related work) has submitted their independent review. Here is their full assessment. Please read it and prepare a brief response (under 300 words) noting:\n1. Which of R2's points you agree with\n2. Which you disagree with and why\n3. Whether R2's observations change your assessment in any way\n\n---\n\n**R2's Review (Score: 2/6 Reject, Confidence: 4/5)**\n\n**Strengths (R2 perspective):**\n- Well-isolated curated-vs-random experimental design\n- Practically relevant negative result\n- LoRA capacity artifact is an interesting observation\n- Format-level metrics fill a real gap\n\n**Key Weaknesses (R2 perspective):**\n1. **Extremely thin related work** — only 11 references. Missing: iterative DPO/self-play (Yuan et al. 2024, Chen et al. 2024, Singh et al. 2024), diversity in RLHF (Kirk et al. 2024), reward overoptimization (Gao et al. 2023), broader collapse literature (Seddik et al. 2024, Gerstgrasser et al. 2024), diversity metrics (Li et al. distinct-n, BERTScore).\n2. **Novelty limited to negative result at toy scale** — 0.6B-1.5B is far from practical alignment scale (7B-70B+).\n3. **\"Cross-architecture\" claim is misleading** — both models are from Qwen family, not truly different architectures.\n4. **Semantic metrics may be insensitive by construction** — Vendi Score blindness (their own Finding 4) may extend more broadly. Self-BLEU 0.005-0.007 is near-floor.\n5. **No quality evaluation** — diversity is preserved but no quality benchmarks to show curation is actually doing something useful.\n6. **Format metrics narrowly scoped** — only first 20-30 tokens.\n7. **No statistical rigor** — single runs, no confidence intervals.\n8. **CARR mention underdeveloped** — mentioned in discussion but not developed.\n\n**R2 Questions:**\n- Have you validated Vendi Score sensitivity (e.g., artificial deduplication)?\n- Scale extrapolation basis for 7B+ claims?\n- How many random seeds per config?\n- Quality metrics across generations?\n- Why only 11 references?\n- Can Qwen3-0.6B vs Qwen2.5-1.5B really be called \"cross-architecture\"?\n\n---\n\nPlease respond with your reaction to R2's points."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5740,"cache_read_input_tokens":48075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5740},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92cca1d5-ce22-4ffe-a33d-e2fb8f40ddd5","uuid":"8df71862-8a2a-4a5f-bcf5-1cb879a1ad1a"}
